Package: omopduckdb
Title: Build and Populate an OMOP CDM v5.4 Database in DuckDB
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("J Kyle", "Armstrong", email = "j.kyle.armstrong@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4269-0121"))
Description: Tools for building an OMOP Common Data Model (CDM) v5.4 schema
    in DuckDB, loading the OHDSI Athena vocabulary (from a local download or
    live from BigQuery), and mapping PCORnet-format source data into the CDM
    via parallel R and Python ETL implementations that share the same
    concept-mapping SQL. Also includes a Google Drive sync helper for the
    large generated database/vocabulary files.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    DBI,
    duckdb,
    stringr,
    yaml
Suggests:
    googledrive,
    bigrquery,
    CommonDataModel,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
